@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using global::Crest.Site.Client

@*
    Mounted via Startup.cs's routes.MapRazorComponents<App>() (Phase 3.5's interactive-
    island mechanism) - this is the actual root component for any @rendermode-marked
    page such as wasm/Pages/BlazorCounter.razor. Static-SSR-only content (the
    overwhelming majority) never goes through this at all; it's served directly by
    CrestBlazorComponentShapeBindingResolver's HtmlRenderer path mid-shape, with no
    App/Routes involvement. Kept minimal on purpose: Layout.liquid's actual <head>/<body>
    shape (resource manifests, culture attributes, nav) gets ported to a Razor layout
    component in Phase 5, not duplicated here ahead of time.

    Routes (and every routable @page component, e.g. BlazorCounter.razor) lives in the
    .Client (WASM) project, not here - the WASM runtime downloaded to the browser only
    has whatever assembly it was itself compiled into, never this server assembly, so a
    Routes defined here would resolve fine over the SignalR circuit but throw
    "Root component type ... could not be found" the moment InteractiveAuto switches to
    WASM. See docs/BlazorWeb.md.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="RenderMode.InteractiveAuto" />
</head>
<body>
    <Routes @rendermode="RenderMode.InteractiveAuto" />
    <script src="/_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
